-- Lay many frames of one sky on each other: trails, or a stack.
--
-- Two things a tripod and a dark hour make possible. TRAILS keeps
-- whatever is brightest with the frames left where they were, so the
-- sky's own motion draws the picture. A STACK registers the frames on
-- the stars and averages them, buying the signal-to-noise of one long
-- exposure without its blown highlights or its trailing -- and the
-- clipped mode leaves out whatever the stack disagrees with, which is
-- what a satellite, an aeroplane and a cosmic ray all are.
--
-- The registration leans on the one thing the sky is honest about: it
-- turns at a constant rate. Given a focal length and the frames' own
-- timestamps, there is an upper bound on how far anything can have
-- moved, so the first pair is solved inside a disc of known radius
-- rather than an unbounded plane -- by voting, since every pair of
-- stars implies a shift and the true one is what many pairs agree on.
-- Once one pair is solved the drift is a vector per second, and every
-- later frame is predicted rather than searched.
--
-- Deterministic end to end: no model is asked for anything.

param photos: text = "."
param pattern: text = "*.RAF"
param mode: text = "trails"
param only: text = ""
param focal_mm: num = 0
param sensor_mm: num = 23.5
param darks: text = ""
param flats: text = ""
param bias: text = ""
param sigma: num = 2.5
param output: text = ""
param demosaic: bool = true

use python "superimpose_kernel.py"

-- Where every frame sits relative to the first. Trails ignores this;
-- a stack cannot be honest without it.
placed := register(photos, pattern, only, focal_mm, sensor_mm, demosaic)

-- What the sky was doing while each frame was open. Cloud hides
-- stars and brightens the background, and both were already measured
-- by the pass that registered -- so setting aside the frames the sky
-- ruined costs nothing and no model is asked.
screened := screen_frames(placed)
print(screen_note(screened))

-- The frames laid on each other, the way the mode asks for.
stacked := superimpose(screened, mode, output, darks, sigma, flats, bias)
check stack_valid(stacked)
print(stack_note(stacked))

-- The report lands beside the stack it describes.
where := stack_home(stacked)
check stack_valid(stacked)
act file.overwrite(where, stacked)
settle until check file_exists(where) within 5
commit(stacked)
